services: correct legacy scheduler announcement name length

Issue #4 legacy announcement transition.

The pre-protocol-38 ICE packet now serializes its one-byte netname length
with the historical receiver contract: the length includes the trailing NUL.
The encoder uses unsigned byte arithmetic, preserves the native-endian legacy
start-time field, accepts an empty name without underflow, and truncates longer
names deterministically to the maximum representable 254 bytes.

The packet construction is isolated in a pure module so ordinary, empty, and
maximum-length round trips are checked without network timing.  An exact
historical off-by-one mutant must fail at complete-name preservation and at the
255-byte boundary.  The executor also reruns every landed protocol-neutral
issue-4 gate and negative control before committing.
